course: dictionary
lesson: 8373
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change meaning depending on where they sit in a sentence. The context tells you which meaning the author means. In «Routines save time and help you remember things», routine means the usual order of things you do every day.
explain: A routine is the order you do things in, like a morning routine: wake up, wash, dress, eat breakfast. In «a routine check-up», routine is an adjective, and it means ordinary, regular and normal. Check the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: Look for clue words such as usual, daily, every day and same time. In «keeping usual routines and giving yourself time make them feel normal again», the word usual tells you a routine is something you keep doing as normal. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: A routine is the usual order in which you do things, such as a morning routine or a bedtime routine.
fact: «Routines save time and stop you forgetting things» because you do not have to decide each step.
fact: A routine can also be a set of movements that have been practised, such as a dance or gymnastics routine.
fact: As an adjective, routine means ordinary, regular and normal, as in «a routine check-up».
fact: In computing, a routine is a set of instructions.
exercise: «Routines save time and help you remember things.» What does routines mean here? | A kind of dance | Places you visit on holiday | A long, boring story | *The usual order of things you do every day
exercise: Mia says a dance routine is a fancy hat. What is a dance routine? | *A set of dance movements that have been practised and performed | A dance shoe | A kind of music | A prize for winning a race
exercise: «Ella had a routine check-up at the dentist.» In this sentence, routine means: | *Ordinary, regular and normal | Very old | Hidden under the bed | Angry and loud
test: «Dogs learn daily routines and may notice how a person's smell fades in the house during the day.» Which word in this sentence tells you routines happen every day? | Smell | *Daily | Fades | Learn
test: Which sentence uses routine to mean ordinary and normal? | *The doctor said my check-up was routine, so there was nothing to worry about. | I follow my bedtime routine every night. | She learned a new routine for the gym.
exam: Read «Keeping usual routines helps big changes feel normal again.» What does routines mean here, and which word is the clue? | *The usual order of things you do; the clue is usual | Instructions for a computer; the clue is feel | Dances on a stage; the clue is changes | The lessons at school; the clue is big
